  "pairing": "bitter-karla",
  "typeCharacter": "Bitter is a sturdy, warm slab serif with the feel of a carved wooden house sign. It is set in heavy weight, sentence case and very large (the h1 is about 7vw, section headings about 3.5vw, the apartment numerals 2 and 4 at about 11vw), while Karla carries the running text at 18px regular, with small Karla medium labels in sentence case only and no tracking.",
  "composition": "Hero: a full-width deep green #12403f field. Across its upper third runs a painted linocut ridge of the Vogel mountains in pale teal #8cc2ba and #e6f0ee on the dark ground, edge to edge. Under the ridge the h1 sits left-aligned over columns 1 to 9, the lead over columns 1 to 6 and one red #b23f28 button with square corners beneath it. Columns 10 to 12 hold the phone as a large Bitter numeral in #e6f0ee. At the bottom of the hero comes the signature schematic: a thin horizontal #8cc2ba line across all 12 columns, starting at a small square marker (the house, labelled Ukanc), dashed in the middle with a 300 m label and ending in a flat teal lake shape at the right edge. Rooms, on the light #eef4f3 ground: the heading sits over columns 1 to 6, then two columns of six, each starting with a huge Bitter numeral, 2 and 4, in #12403f, followed by a short title, a list (kuhinja, kopalnica, balkon, WiFi, parkirišče) and thin #c6d6d4 rules between items, with a vertical rule between the two. Story, on a white #ffffff section: text over columns 1 to 6 and a painted ink spruce sprig with gentian flowers over columns 8 to 12. Highlights: a full-width #12403f ribbon of short words in Karla, #e6f0ee (Vogel, Savica, psi po dogovoru, English, Deutsch, italiano), followed on the light ground by a two-column list of the four highlights with slab-serif lead words. Call: a deep #12403f field with the heading and email over columns 1 to 6, one red button, and a simple schematic map in teal lines over columns 8 to 12 showing the western tip of the lake with a dot for Ukanc 18, plus the address underneath.",
  "imagery": "No photographs at all. The imagery is two painted pieces: a wide linocut-style band of the Vogel ridge with layered peaks in pale teal tones on the flat deep-green hero ground, and an ink-and-wash botanical of a spruce sprig with blue gentian on plain white in the story section. Neither piece contains letters, buildings, people or signs. Everything else is drawn with rules and schematics: the 300 m walking line and the lake-end map, in thin teal strokes.",
  "signature": "The 300 m line under the mountain: a single schematic walk at the foot of the hero, running from the house in Ukanc to the lake, beneath the painted Vogel ridge.",
  "copy": {
    "headline": "Na koncu Bohinjskega jezera, pod Voglom",
    "lead": "Smo Marko in Petra Zupan. V naši hiši v Ukancu oddajamo tri apartmaje s kuhinjo, kopalnico in balkonom, do jezera pa je le 300 m peš."
  },
  "imagePrompt": "One flat full-page screenshot of a desktop website homepage, 1536x1024 px, with no browser window, no device frame and no perspective. Clean, bold alpine-guesthouse design on a 12-column grid. Typography: Bitter, a heavy warm slab serif, for headings in sentence case and very large; Karla, a friendly sans, for body text. HERO (about the top 55%): a full-width flat deep green #12403f field. Across its upper third runs a wide linocut-style painting of a mountain ridge (the Vogel range above Lake Bohinj), with layered jagged peaks carved in pale teal #8cc2ba and soft #e6f0ee on the flat dark green, spanning edge to edge, with no text, buildings or people in it. Below the ridge, left-aligned over about 9 columns, is a huge heavy Bitter headline in #e6f0ee, then a short Karla lead in #e6f0ee over 6 columns, then one rectangular red #b23f28 button with square corners and #f6f8f7 text. At the right, over columns 10 to 12, is a phone number set as a large Bitter numeral in #e6f0ee. At the very bottom of the hero, a thin teal #8cc2ba horizontal line crosses the full width: it starts at the left with a small square marker and a small label, turns dashed in the middle with a small distance label, and ends on the right in a flat teal lake shape. ROOMS: a light cool #eef4f3 ground. A Bitter heading in #16262a sits top left, then two equal columns divided by a thin #c6d6d4 vertical rule. Each column opens with an enormous Bitter numeral in #12403f (2 on the left, 4 on the right), then a short title and a short list separated by thin #c6d6d4 rules, in Karla #16262a and #4a5f62. STORY (partly visible at the bottom): a white #ffffff section with Karla body text and a Bitter heading on the left half, and on the right an ink-and-wash botanical painting of a spruce sprig with blue gentian flowers on plain white, with no letters in it. Flat colours only: no gradients, no shadows, no photographs, no faces, no rounded pill buttons, nothing centred. The layout is asymmetric, generous and immersive."
}

